From 3c75c449366daf3d93133d8d824c732c750ad92d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maxime <maxime.lefrancois@emse.fr>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:39:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Natural datatype of JSON integers (RML-Core)

RML-Core gives a reference its natural RDF literal: a JSON integer gives
"30"^^xsd:integer. The CG test cases expect it since
kg-construct/rml-core#218 (e.g. RMLTC0002a, 0007c-f, 0008a-b, 0011b, 0012a);
the values were simple literals.

The parser now types the literal references of a JSON source whose values
are all integers (the dtype of the column read), as it already does for
RDB columns, in mappings written in the vocabulary of the W3C KG-Construct
CG only: legacy RML and R2RML references keep simple literals, as
RMLio/rml-test-cases expects. Doubles and booleans are not typed yet (their
lexical forms would need converting too). Each JSON source is read once.

Tests: test/json-natural-datatypes (a CG mapping and a legacy one); the
expected outputs of the copied RML-Core cases RMLTC0002a, 0007c-f, 0008a-b,
0011b and 0012a (test/rml-core/json) are those of the current CG suite.
